    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Ninth Speech: A Response to Bildad"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Job spoke again:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“How you have helped the powerless!",
          "How you have saved the weak!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How you have enlightened my stupidity!",
          "What wise advice you have offered!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Where have you gotten all these wise sayings?",
          "Whose spirit speaks through you?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“The dead tremble—",
          "those who live beneath the waters."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The underworld is naked in God’s presence.",
          "The place of destruction is uncovered."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God stretches the northern sky over empty space",
          "and hangs the earth on nothing."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He wraps the rain in his thick clouds,",
          "and the clouds don’t burst with the weight."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He covers the face of the moon,",
          "shrouding it with his clouds."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He created the horizon when he separated the waters;",
          "he set the boundary between day and night."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The foundations of heaven tremble;",
          "they shudder at his rebuke."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "By his power the sea grew calm.",
          "By his skill he crushed the great sea monster."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His Spirit made the heavens beautiful,",
          "and his power pierced the gliding serpent."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "These are just the beginning of all that he does,",
          "merely a whisper of his power.",
          "Who, then, can comprehend the thunder of his power?”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
